      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T18:31:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`aarch64` was the default arch prior to this CL and the `-a` flag is not being used in the `aarch64/build.sh`. Only in the `x86_64/build.sh` we set `-a x86_64`.\n\nMy thought was to make Kokoro\u0027s `build.sh` script platform independent to reduce maintenance burden -- the same exact build script will run on any (supported) platform and generate an image file for that platform. Just like `apt install X` makes Debian install the `X` package for the right machine arch without us having to explicitly specify it.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "1b3e1527_a66defcb",
      "revId": "ccb4fb6fb6cd883332584e7778dc8b0f64483306",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
